@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# Mailchimp customer sync boundary
+
+Research note for the customer sync boundary required before any Mailchimp
+connector is built. Live integration and bulk export of real customer lists
+are out of scope.
+
+## 1. Marketing sync is opt-in and disabled by default
+
+Marketing sync is opt-in per store and disabled by default. No customer is
+pushed to Mailchimp until:
+
+1. the store enables the Mailchimp integration, and
+2. the customer has given explicit, recorded consent for marketing email.
+
+Absence of consent is treated as "do not export", not as an error.
+
+## 2. Official Mailchimp API documentation
+
+| Concern | Endpoint | Docs |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Audiences | `/3.0/lists` | https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/audiences/ |
+| Contacts (audience members) | `/3.0/lists/{list_id}/members` | https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/list-members/ |
+| Consent fields | `marketing_permissions` on member create/update | https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/list-members/ |
+| Tags | `/3.0/lists/{list_id}/members/{subscriber_hash}/tags` | https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/list-member-tags/ |
+| Unsubscribe handling | member `status` transitions (`subscribed` -> `unsubscribed`) | https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/list-members/update-list-member/ |
+
+Audience members are identified by `email_address`; Posnic's own
+`external_id` is carried as a merge field so the mapping survives an email
+change on Posnic's side.
+
+## 3. Field export matrix
+
+### Required consent: overall opt-in
+
+- `email_address`
+- `status` (`subscribed` only, never `transactional`)
+
+### Exportable with the store-level opt-in
+
+- `external_id` (Posnic customer id, as a merge field)
+- `merge_fields.FNAME`, `merge_fields.LNAME`
+- `merge_fields.LOCALE`
+
+### Requires explicit per-customer marketing consent
+
+Marketing consent is stored per channel and must be present before these are
+sent:
+
+- `marketing_permissions` (`marketing_permissions[].marketing_permission_id`
+  + `enabled`)
+- `tags`
+- `merge_fields.BIRTHDAY`
+- `merge_fields.PHONE` (SMS channel only)
+- purchase/engagement history
+
+### Never exported
+
+- payment card data, bank details
+- passwords, API keys, auth tokens
+- free-text order or support notes
+- government identifiers
+
+## 4. Synthetic sync fixture
+
+Synthetic only; no real customer data.
+
+```json
+{
+  "store_id": "store_synthetic_001",
+  "audience_id": "aud_synthetic_0001",
+  "customer": {
+    "external_id": "posnic_cust_0001",
+    "email_address": "ada.lovelace@example.test",
+    "merge_fields": {
+      "FNAME": "Ada",
+      "LNAME": "Lovelace",
+      "LOCALE": "en"
+    },
+    "marketing_consent": {
+      "email": true,
+      "sms": false,
+      "marketing_permission_id": "perm_synthetic_01",
+      "consented_at": "2026-01-05T10:00:00Z",
+      "source": "in_store_signup"
+    }
+  },
+  "tags": ["loyalty"],
+  "status": "subscribed"
+}
+```
+
+## 5. Unsubscribe handling
+
+Unsubscribes originate in Mailchimp. Posnic must consume the `unsubscribed`
+webhook ([list member events](https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/list-member-events/))
+and record the change locally; Posnic must never re-subscribe a contact whose
+`status` is `unsubscribed` or `cleaned` without a fresh consent event.
```

